Adds src/hooks/useUrlFilters: a small hook that persists a set of string filters in
the URL query string so admin list views are deep-linkable and reload-safe, the
foundation the week board (N-5) and notification deep-links build on. setFilters
patches one-or-more keys in a SINGLE history-replace so clearing several filters can't
race a stale snapshot; empty/default values are omitted; scroll position preserved.

Wires it into the inventory list (the richest filter set — 5 dropdowns — so it stresses
the abstraction) with the values aliased to the old names so reads/load() are untouched;
only the setters changed. search + pagination stay local for now. The page body is
wrapped in <Suspense> (required by Next 16 for useSearchParams — mirrors
src/app/setup-account/page.tsx; without it next build fails).

4-agent review:
- antagonist (BLOCKER, fixed): useSearchParams needs a Suspense boundary or the build
  fails — added, matching the app's existing pattern. Also memoized the returned filters
  object (footgun for future callers). Confirmed: no refetch loop, clear-all race genuinely
  fixed, no key collisions, no hydration mismatch, operator read-only parity preserved.
- product/operator-lens (KEY, sequencing): this slice is plumbing without a consumer —
  ~0 manager-hours until something emits a filtered URL. NEXT (do before more inventory
  polish): (1) wire LOW_INVENTORY notification (alert-display.ts dead-ends on the
  unfiltered list) to a pre-filtered URL; (2) persist search in the URL (debounced) so
  reload doesn't silently drop it; (3) roll the hook to /admin/deployments + /admin/requests
  (the week board + bell's real click-through targets); (4) a filtered-state banner so a
  short deep-linked list doesn't read as missing data.

VERIFY IN CC (not provable in-sandbox — no next build): npm run build succeeds (the
Suspense requirement), and a deep-link like /admin/inventory?hubId=<id> lands pre-filtered.
